---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ApiDocGenerator from '../../components/ApiDocGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="API Endpoint Documentation Generator"
  description="Fill in a method, path, parameters, and example response to instantly generate clean Markdown API documentation."
>
  <ApiDocGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Consistent docs, less typing</h2>
  <p>
    Writing API documentation by hand often means retyping the same
    Markdown table structure for every endpoint. This tool takes structured
    input — method, path, parameters, example response — and generates
    consistently formatted Markdown you can drop straight into a README or
    docs site.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Fill in the HTTP method, path, and a one-line description.</li>
    <li>List parameters as <code>name: type — description</code>, one per line.</li>
    <li>Paste an example JSON response.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated Markdown.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>API Doc Generator FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this validate my JSON?</strong> No — it's inserted as-is
    into a code block. Format it correctly before pasting for best results.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Can I document multiple endpoints at once?</strong> Generate one
    endpoint at a time and combine the outputs — this keeps each block
    focused and easy to review before assembling a full API reference.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does it support authentication documentation?</strong> Not as a
    dedicated field — describe auth requirements in the endpoint description,
    or add a separate section covering auth that applies across endpoints.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
